# SpendSmart on GCP VM (existing Kubernetes)

The server already runs Kubernetes. **Postgres + ClickHouse** live in the `databases` namespace; the app is installed with the **Helm chart** only.

## Prerequisites

- Working `kubectl` / `KUBECONFIG`
- Firewall: **TCP 30080–30083** (NodePorts)
- Harbor access from nodes (for private images)

## First-time: in-cluster databases (once)

```bash
cp deploy/harbor.env.example deploy/harbor.env   # optional, for image pulls
bash scripts/vm/create-harbor-pull-secret.sh databases
bash scripts/vm/bootstrap-databases.sh
# passwords → deploy/.db.generated.env (or copy to deploy/db.env)
```

## Deploy / upgrade (Helm only)

```bash
cp deploy/gpg.env.example deploy/gpg.env
cp deploy/vm.env.example deploy/vm.env           # PUBLIC_HOST, IMAGE_TAG
bash scripts/vm/one-click-deploy.sh
```

Or: `bash scripts/vm/deploy-spendsmart.sh`

Open: `http://<PUBLIC_HOST>:30080`

## Scripts

| Script | Role |
|--------|------|
| `scripts/vm/one-click-deploy.sh` | Helm deploy (checks cluster) |
| `scripts/vm/deploy-spendsmart.sh` | Secrets + `helm upgrade --install` |
| `scripts/vm/bootstrap-databases.sh` | Postgres + ClickHouse (one-time) |
| `scripts/vm/create-harbor-pull-secret.sh` | `harbor-regcred` |

Chart: `charts/spendsmart` with `-f values-vm.yaml`.